# No-Wrapper / No-Alias Rule (BE + FE)

<!-- GEN: Why: shims and aliases hide where code really lives and outlive their "temporary" label. Kind: Suggested — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Recommended for every project. If the project already has such a rule (P5), keep its exact content and translate only. Adapt the examples to the stack (Python aliases, TS re-exports...). -->

**One concept = one location.** Callers call the canonical location directly.

## Forbidden

1. Pass-through functions/methods that only call another function without adding logic.
2. Re-export / compatibility shim files ({{be_shim_examples}}; {{fe_shim_examples}}).
3. Aliases kept for an old name (`import x as y`, `export { x as y }`, `y = x`).
4. Wrapper classes/hooks/components that only forward props or calls.
5. New code importing back into an old path.
6. "Temporary" compatibility shims — no exception.

## Required when moving code

- Move + fix every caller (app + tests) + delete the old file in the same phase.
- Confirm with `grep` that 0 imports point at the old path.

## Allowed

- Functions/hooks/components adding real behavior (validation, authorization, transactions, real mapping, caching).
- Ports with ≥ 2 implementations or an approved test boundary.
- The valid barrels listed in `fe/05-dependency-rules.md`; empty `__init__.py`; framework entrypoints.

